good afternoon chair members of the committee for the record my name is Rachel Irwing land development and permitting program manager for the Cheyenne region uh our address is 1 Microsoft Way Redmond Washington today's request includes three actions for Highlands annexation into the city of Cheyenne reszoning the property to business park and a future land use amendment i'd like to give a quick overview of the project uh Highlands is a 3,50 acre property with an existing Microsoft campus and planned conservation area to the west gravel pits to the north a planned solar farm to the east and state land to the south i do want to note that Microsoft does not yet own this property the site is currently going through our acquisition process and

these applications are part of early stage planning with that being said we are working to close on this property in the coming weeks because of this our goal here today is transparency i've brought a few of our subject matter experts with me today from our water wastewater energy and community affairs team uh so that we can do our absolute best to answer any questions that you may have and also be clear about what we know today and what we will know in the future as our project is refined and progresses that same approach to transparency is how we've been engaging with the community as well on May 27th as Brad was stating we did hold a neighborhood meeting for the those surrounding the Highland property where we had the opportunity to answer questions directly uh

the following day on May 28th we did host a public community openhouse that had roughly 150 attendees where we shared our expansion plans and had subject matter experts available to respond to any questions we plan to continue those community engagements throughout the summer to ensure residents have the opportunity to bring forward questions and concerns because we do want community and city input um to be involved in the shaping of our plans moving forward one of the most consistent questions we've heard to date is why is the site so large and why are these approvals being requested now Highlands is a long-term planning effort um not an immediate full buildout of the campus development of this site may occur over 10 to 20 years as infrastructure technology and

demand evolve and while you may not see work directly on the property in the near term that does not mean that work wouldn't have begun uh that site likely will require significant off-site improvements including wet utility roadway and power upgrades which we anticipate advancing ahead of any vertical data center construction to properly support future development planning at the full parcel scale allows Microsoft and the city to work holistically on these infrastructure improvements rather than approaching these decisions in a fragmented way over time it also allows the city into the process significantly earlier when those decisions can still be shaped collaboratively annexation ensures that this project be developed under city standards and within city jurisdiction allowing for coordinated planning with the city and

