one of the a couple of interesting things about the LPCS uh one of them it does require us to directly pay for 100% of the infrastructure upgrades that are required to support our uh growth and our data centers we have to pay for 100% of the power that's procured or generated to provide electricity to our data centers the other thing that's unique about this tariff is that it does enable the utility to call on our backup generators in the event of a grid emergency so if the market power is tight or there's some generation outages in the region utility has the option to call on Microsoft to shed load to backup generators before curtailing hospitals nursing homes schools and

